abstract: "Bank statement analysis turns months of statement rows into the figures a lender, court or auditor asks for: deposits after taking out transfers between your own accounts, withdrawals, month-end, lowest and average daily balances, NSF and overdraft items, large deposits and the payers who come back every month. This repo has a summary template, a fictional three-month sample, and a script that builds the summary from converted statement rows and checks each month against the printed balances first. Version 1.1.0 adds a spec defining every figure, JSON Schemas, eleven rules with IDs, and a checker that matches own-account transfers across accounts and builds per-account and all-accounts figures."
